  "caveats": [
    "hatir/twin numbers are exploration-grade/RELATIVE (ranking + crossover, not silicon-accurate absolutes); only ratios and crossover positions are promoted to text.",
    "The 6 papers do NOT publish H100 wall-clock decode; absolute us/token is a roofline lower bound, externally unverifiable, deferred to the in-house A100 runbook (Part III-a).",
    "Per-kernel roofline only: no kernel-launch/scheduling/tail-effect overheads.",
    "KV comparison assumes GQA-8 / head-dim 128 (kv_dim=1024); MHA and other GQA groups shift S* linearly (see S_star.kv_dim_d_MHA column).",
    "State multipliers m are from published architecture descriptions (2-layer MLP=8d^2, +momentum=16d^2), not from released decode traces; HOPE m is the fastest-level per-token portion, total resident state across ~6 CMS levels is larger and mostly low-frequency.",
    "C* uses a matrix-memory (W in R^{dxd}) chunkwise intensity model; a 2-layer MLP memory scales FLOPs and bytes together, preserving the curve SHAPE but not the exact C* value.",
    "(d,L) per param scale are canonical transformer shapes, not the exact per-paper configs (most papers report params, not full width/depth); the 1.3B anchor matches the plan."
  ]
